" tridactylrc — browser bindings that mirror ~/.config/nvim
"
" Tridactyl's rc parser only treats a line STARTING with " as a comment; a
" trailing one becomes part of the command. So every note lives on its own line.
"
" Auto-sourced at startup only when the native messenger is installed
" (:installnative). Without it, run :source by hand.

" ============================================================================
" External editor — the reason for going back to Gecko at all
" ============================================================================
" <C-i> in any text field hands it to nvim. kitty rather than foot: it's the one
" terminal present in both the sway and the i3 session. Tridactyl appends the
" temp filename as the last argument.
"
" --class gives the window its own app_id (Wayland) / WM_CLASS (X11) so the WM
" can float it instead of tiling it into whatever you were reading. The matching
" for_window rules live in linux/.config/{sway,i3}/config. -e must come last.
set editorcmd kitty --class tridactyl-editor -e nvim

" ============================================================================
" Find — nvim <leader>/ (fuzzy in buffer), n/N
" ============================================================================
bind <Space>/ fillcmdline find
bind n findnext 1
bind N findnext -1

" ============================================================================
" Tabs as buffers — nvim <leader>p pickers, <leader>bd
" ============================================================================
" <leader>pf: fff.nvim find_files -> every tab in every window
bind <Space>pf fillcmdline taball
" <leader>pb: telescope buffers -> tabs in this window
bind <Space>pb fillcmdline tab
" <leader>pr: telescope oldfiles -> reopen a recently closed tab
bind <Space>pr fillcmdline undo
" <leader>bd: Snacks.bufdelete
bind <Space>bd tabclose
" <leader>w: save -> the browser's version of keeping it
bind <Space>w bmark

" ============================================================================
" Swap — nvim <leader>x group
" ============================================================================
bind <Space>xh tabmove -1
bind <Space>xl tabmove +1

" ============================================================================
" Search/help — nvim <leader>ps group
" ============================================================================
" <leader>psh: telescope help_tags
bind <Space>psh fillcmdline help
" <leader>psk: telescope keymaps
bind <Space>psk fillcmdline_notrail bind

" ============================================================================
" Reload this file — nvim's config-reload habit
" ============================================================================
bind <Space>vr source

" ============================================================================
" Deliberately NOT rebound
" ============================================================================
" ]] and [[ default to `followpage next|prev`, which is a better browser
" analogue of nvim's next/prev-reference than tab cycling would be. gt/gT
" already cycle tabs.
"
" <C-d>/<C-u> already scroll half a page. nvim recentres after them (zz);
" a web page has no cursor to centre on, so there is nothing to mirror.
"
" Zen's own compact-mode keys are separate from Tridactyl and still work:
" Ctrl+Alt+S reveals the sidebar, Ctrl+S toggles compact mode.
